# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch notes. TEMPORARY/ is the working directory for session-specific
# staging notes - things that are true for one afternoon and misleading a week
# later. Keeping them out of the repository is deliberate: a future session
# reading stale notes as if they were documentation is worse than having none.
# Anything worth keeping graduates into docs/ and gets committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEMPORARY/
TEMP_NOTES.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Secrets. Nothing in this repo should need one, which is why any that appear
# must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Per-machine model selection (ROADMAP section 8). The committed roster is the
# default; this file is one machine's override and describes that machine.
ai-org-router/config/local_models.yaml

# Model weights. Gigabytes each, and pulled by a person, never committed.
*.gguf
*.safetensors

# VS Code extension packaging (paladin-vscode)
node_modules/
*.vsix

# Editor / OS / local tool settings
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.claude/settings.local.json

# NOT ignored on purpose: ai-org-router/logs/*.jsonl and logs/server.log are
# tracked as demo evidence (see stop_demo.sh). Do not add logs/ here.
